        "type": "slimmer",
        "tekst": "**In plain words**\n\nSome systems are almost impossible to move up in: slavery, the medieval estates and the caste system, where birth decides your job, your partner and who you can mix with. The class system is more open: education and work let you move up or down, but inequality stays. South Africa shows how a race-based system can turn into a class-based one that is still very unequal."
